    "updated_at": "2026-09-24T21:43:44Z",
    "body": "### Reproduction\n\n**Environment**\n- OS: Ubuntu 24.04.4 LTS (Noble Numbat)\n- Python: 3.12.9\n- pytest: 9.1.1\n- Commit: `2f4e82f52efbcfcc57d65b3fa5348672163ca088`\n- Working tree: clean\n\n**Steps to reproduce**\n\nI cloned my fork, followed the repository README setup instructions, and activated the project's virtual environment.\n\nI first ran:\n\n```bash\npytest tests/unit/test_readme_scorer.py -q\n\nThis completed with:\n22 passed, 1 xfailed\n\nI then ran pytest tests/unit/test_readme_scorer.py::TestReadmeScorer::test_readme_with_all_quality_signals -q --runxfail:\n\nThis failed at:\nassert data[\"word_count\"] > 100 with assert 51 > 100\n\nThe scorer also reports:\n\nword_count=51\ncategory=minimal\n\n**Expected result**\n\nThe test expects the README fixture to be categorized as:\n\n\nThe scorer categorizes word counts below 100 as minimal, 100 through 499 as adequate, and 500 or more as comprehensive.\n\n**Evidence**\n\nThe current fixture produces a word count of 51, so it cannot satisfy the test later expectation that word_count_category == comprehensive.\n\nI was able to reproduce the reported behavior consistently on the commit and environment listed above.",
